## Using sftp from pc to z/OS                                           00010000
                                                                        00020000
### Using sftp on PC                                                    00030000
                                                                        00040000
Using Port 2022 and then your userid followed by the cbt IP address. In 00050000
this example I'm using a hostname I've defined in my PC's hostname file 00060000
so I don't have to remember the IP address.                             00070000
                                                                        00080000
Then using the `ls /+` syntax define the DCB and dsorg.                 00090000
                                                                        00100000
Next change the remote location to my TSO hlq and `put` the file.       00110000
                                                                        00120000
*Note* by default `sftp` does a binary transfer, use `ls /+ mode=text`  00130000
to do a text transfer.                                                  00140000
                                                                        00150000
                                                                        00160000
```                                                                     00170000
d:\temp>sftp -P 2022 lbdyck1@cbt                                        00180000
lbdyck1@cbt's password:                                                 00190000
Connected to cbt.                                                       00200000
sftp> ls /+ recfm=-fb,lrecl=80,blksize=0,dsorg=ps                       00210000
/+/blksize=0     /+/dsorg=ps      /+/error.log     /+/gdgnt             00220000
/+/ispfenq       /+/ispfstats     /+/loglevel=I                         00230000
/+/lrecl=80      /+/mode=binary                                         00240000
sftp> cd //lbdyck1                                                      00250000
sftp> put VUELOAD.xmi*                                                  00260000
Uploading VUELOAD.xmit to //LBDYCK1/VUELOAD.xmit                        00270000
VUELOAD.xmit                               00%  709KB   1.1MB/s   00:00 00280000
sftp> quit                                                              00290000
```                                                                     00300000
                                                                        00310000
